# UI kit (stack)

- Reach for Mantine components and hooks first; don't reinvent what the kit provides. Override via Mantine's style props / `classNames` API, not by fighting Mantine internals with Tailwind (see `stack/tailwind`, `stack/css`).
- Style variants via `class-variance-authority` + `tailwind-merge` routed through the project's `cn` helper; don't scatter raw `clsx`/`twMerge` calls (see `stack/tailwind`).
- Forms: Mantine inputs wired through the `mantine-form` adapter; wire `label`/`error` props — don't strip them for layout. Form driver is React Hook Form (see `stack/react`); schemas are Zod (see `stack/api`).
- Don't break Mantine's a11y when overriding: keep `role`, `aria-*`, and keyboard handlers intact (see `stack/accessibility`).
